            "review_title": "Review at Vit 29 Restaurant",
            "review_text": "G C\nAnchorage, Alaska966 contributions\n0\nDelicious roasted duck, served in many different ways :)\nMay 2015 • Solo\nThe Quan Vit 29 restaurant is a great spot in the Old Quarter to taste roasted duck, and they offer a big variety of dishes that features this very tasty food :)) There are several of these in Ha Noi, and I've eaten at the one located at 24 Nguyen Huu Huan many times -- and have experienced very polite and friendly service, plus consistently well-prepared meals (reasonably priced) on every occasion. There are a few folks on their staff who can speak English... but don't worry about language barriers, as they have a nice menu with good photos of their offerings. There are good choices for solo diners and groups too... I usually order the delicious sticky rice and their salad (made with fresh shredded veggies, with slices of duck, and served with a sweet-tangy dressing... it sort of resembles cole slaw, but it much tastier :). Of course, their whole roasted duck, chopped into pieces for easy consumption, is their hallmark dish (lots of folks get this to go as well). I've seen very few tourists here -- the diners are usually entirely local Vietnamese folks, and it gets very busy during the lunch hour, which is a testimony to their yummy food. Enjoy the Quan Vit 29, as I frequently do :))\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten May 18, 2015",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
