            "review_text": "JeanGourmet\nParis, France14 contributions\n0\nAn excellent place for duck-lovers.remince\nNov 2013 • Friends\nWe we're taken here by a Vietnamese friend. The restaurant only serves duck - \"vit\" in Vietnamese. We had the crispy roast variety. For three, with vermicelli, soup and pickles, it cost less than fifteen dollars, including beer.\nThe place was full with neighborhood office workers; I suppose there are fewer customers in the evening. It is very simple, with low stools and long tables, bit it looked clean. The tabletops are gleaming stainless steel, and our bowls and chopsticks were presented in sealed plastic bags, apparently sterilized.\n\nIf you like crispy dick, I strongly recommend this place.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 11, 2013",
